module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LimitSectionsCounterexample.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LimitSectionsIdentification.Generator

/-!
# Tag 01Z0 is false at an unrestricted index universe

Tag 01Z0 asserts, of the descent situation of Tag 09RD, that the global sections of the inverse
image of a quasi-coherent module to the limit are the filtered colimit of the global sections of
its inverse images to the later stages.  The unrestricted form of 01Z0 takes the index type and the
  schemes
in **independent** universes and records in its implementation notes that no smallness
assumption on the index type is required.

`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LimitSectionsCounterexample.Basic` builds the counterexample
`Stacks.LimitSectionsCounterexample.collapse` — the spectra of the subrings generated by the finite
  subsets of a
field that is not `u`-small, indexed by those finite subsets — and proves there that it is a
descent situation at 01Z0's own two universes with a non-`u`-small index, that its limit is
the empty scheme, that the apex of 01Z0's cocone is therefore a zero object, so that the
conclusion of 01Z0 forces the colimit of the stagewise sections to be zero, and that the colimit
of the **stage rings** is not zero.  What that file left open, and all it left open, is the
identification of 01Z0's diagram with the diagram of stage rings.  This file supplies that
identification and closes the refutation.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.LimitSectionsIdentification.compHom`: the comparison of the stage ring at `T` with the
  global
  sections of the inverse image of the structure sheaf to the stage `T`.
* `Stacks.LimitSectionsIdentification.groupDiagIso`, `Stacks.LimitSectionsIdentification.diagIso`:
  **the identification**, before and after the universe lift.

## Main results

* `Stacks.LimitSectionsIdentification.compHom_naturality`: the comparison is natural — under it the
  diagram map of 01Z0 is the inclusion of stage rings.
* `Stacks.LimitSectionsIdentification.not_isZero_colimit_pullbackSectionsDiagram`: the colimit of
  the
  diagram of 01Z0 itself is not zero.
* `Stacks.LimitSectionsIdentification.not_isIso_colimitDesc`: **the contradiction.**
* `Stacks.LimitSectionsIdentification.not_card_01Z0`: **Tag 01Z0 is false**, with its conclusion
  quantified over descent situations as the tag states it.

## Route

The identification is assembled from the affine computation of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LimitSectionsIdentification.Generator`, which says that the global
sections of the inverse image of the structure sheaf along `Spec β` are a free module of rank one
on a canonical generator `gen β`, and that the presheaf map of Tag 03DS carries `gen` to `gen`.
Only two things remain here.

First, the diagram of 01Z0 is the composite of `Stacks.LimitSectionsCounterexample.schemesOverBase`
  with the
functor of Tag 03DS, and `AlgebraicGeometry.PullbackSectionsPresheaf.map_objIso` is what ties
that functor's maps to `AlgebraicGeometry.pullbackSectionsMap`; `cardMap_eq` is that step.
Second, the objects and maps of `schemesOverBase collapse` are, definitionally, the
`Over.mk (Spec.map β)` and the `overHom` that the affine computation is stated for; that is
`schemesOverBase_obj` and `schemesOverBase_map`.

The final contradiction does not go through
`Stacks.LimitSectionsCounterexample.not_isZero_colimit_stageSections` as stated, but repeats its
  three-line
argument on the diagram of 01Z0 itself, through `cardCocone`.  The reason is universe-free and
purely about spellings: see the implementation notes.

## Implementation notes

The index of the diagram of 01Z0 is `{i // collapse.base ≤ i}` and the index of
`Stacks.LimitSectionsCounterexample.stageGroupDiagram` is `{T // (∅ : Finset _) ≤ T}`.  These are
  definitionally
equal — `collapse.base` *is* `∅` — but not syntactically, so the `CategoryTheory.Category`
instances on them are different terms, and `CategoryTheory.Limits.HasColimit` is not found for a
diagram carried across the difference.  That is why the contradiction is run on the diagram of
01Z0 itself, where the instance that
  `Stacks.LimitSectionsCounterexample.isZero_colimit_of_isIso_colimitDesc` already
uses is in force, rather than by transporting `IsZero` to the diagram of stage rings.  For the
same reason `simp` and `rw` cannot be used on the naturality goal of `groupDiagIso`, where both
spellings occur: the rewritten goal is not type-correct at `implicit` transparency.  That goal is
discharged by `Eq.trans` against a `congrArg`, which only needs the default transparency.

Two further instance spellings have to be supplied by hand.  Quasi-coherence of the structure
sheaf is not found at the base stage spelled `collapse.system.obj (op collapse.base)`, which is
`isQuasicoherent_structSheaf_collapse`.  And the two `Over`-category objects of
`AlgebraicGeometry.pullbackSectionsMap` are given by name in `transSections`: inferring them from
the expected type leaves a projection applied to a metavariable, and resolving that unfolds
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.pullback`, which is a `CategoryTheory.Functor.leftAdjoint`.

## References

* [The Stacks Project, Tag 01Z0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Z0)
* [The Stacks Project, Tag 09RD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09RD)
* [The Stacks Project, Tag 03DS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DS)
* [The Stacks Project, Tag 06AC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06AC)
-/

@[expose] public section

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
open Stacks.EmptyLimitCounterexample Stacks.LimitSectionsCounterexample

universe u

namespace Stacks.LimitSectionsIdentification

/-- The ring of the base stage of the counterexample. -/
def baseRing : CommRingCat.{u} :=
  CommRingCat.of (stage bigField.{u} (∅ : Finset bigField.{u}))

/-- The index of the diagram of Tag 01Z0: the stages beyond the base stage. -/
abbrev Idx := {T : Finset bigField.{u} // (∅ : Finset bigField.{u}) ≤ T}

/-- The ring of the stage `T`. -/
def stageRing (T : Idx.{u}) : CommRingCat.{u} := CommRingCat.of (stage bigField.{u} T.1)

/-- The inclusion of the base stage ring into the stage ring at `T`. -/
def stageHom (T : Idx.{u}) : baseRing.{u} ⟶ stageRing T :=
  CommRingCat.ofHom (stageMap bigField.{u} T.2)

/-- The inclusion of stage rings along a transition of the index. -/
def transHom {T T' : Idx.{u}} (f : T ⟶ T') : stageRing T ⟶ stageRing T' :=
  CommRingCat.ofHom (stageMap bigField.{u} (leOfHom f))

/-- The unique morphism from the stage `T` to the terminal object over the base stage. -/
theorem stage_w (T : Idx.{u}) :
    Spec.map (stageHom T) ≫ Spec.map (𝟙 baseRing.{u}) = Spec.map (stageHom T) := by
  rw [Spec.map_id, Category.comp_id]

/-- The transitions of the index are compatible with the structure morphisms to the base. -/
theorem trans_w {T T' : Idx.{u}} (f : T ⟶ T') :
    Spec.map (transHom f) ≫ Spec.map (stageHom T) = Spec.map (stageHom T') := by
  rw [← Spec.map_comp]
  exact congrArg Spec.map (ofHom_stageMap_comp bigField.{u} T.2 (leOfHom f)).symm

/-- The object of the diagram at the stage `T` is the spectrum of the stage ring over the base stage. -/
theorem schemesOverBase_obj (T : Idx.{u}) :
    (schemesOverBase collapse.{u}).obj T = op (Over.mk (Spec.map (stageHom T))) := rfl

/-- The transition of the diagram at `f` is the morphism of affine schemes over the base stage induced by
the inclusion of stage rings. -/
theorem schemesOverBase_map {T T' : Idx.{u}} (f : T ⟶ T') :
    (schemesOverBase collapse.{u}).map f =
      (overHom (Spec.map (stageHom T)) (transHom f) (Spec.map (stageHom T'))
        (trans_w f)).op := rfl

/-- The transition map of the diagram of Tag 01Z0 on global sections. -/
def transSections {T T' : Idx.{u}} (f : T ⟶ T') :
    Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (Spec.map (stageHom T))).obj (structSheaf baseRing.{u}), ⊤) ⟶
      Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (Spec.map (stageHom T'))).obj (structSheaf baseRing.{u}), ⊤) :=
  pullbackSectionsMap (structSheaf baseRing.{u})
    (X := Over.mk (Spec.map (stageHom T'))) (Y := Over.mk (Spec.map (stageHom T)))
    (overHom (Spec.map (stageHom T)) (transHom f) (Spec.map (stageHom T')) (trans_w f))

/-- The comparison of the stage ring with the global sections of the inverse image of the
structure sheaf to the stage `T`. -/
def compHom (T : Idx.{u}) :
    (stageGroupDiagram bigField.{u}).obj T ⟶
      Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (Spec.map (stageHom T))).obj (structSheaf baseRing.{u}), ⊤) :=
  genHom (structSheaf baseRing.{u}) (Spec.map (𝟙 baseRing.{u}))
    (structSheafTrivialization baseRing.{u}) (stageHom T) (Spec.map (stageHom T)) (stage_w T)

/-- The comparison `compHom T` is an isomorphism. -/
instance isIso_compHom (T : Idx.{u}) : IsIso (compHom T) :=
  isIso_genHom (structSheaf baseRing.{u}) (Spec.map (𝟙 baseRing.{u}))
    (structSheafTrivialization baseRing.{u}) (stageHom T) (Spec.map (stageHom T)) (stage_w T)

/-- **The comparison is natural**: under it the diagram map of Tag 01Z0 is the inclusion of
stage rings. -/
theorem compHom_naturality {T T' : Idx.{u}} (f : T ⟶ T') :
    (stageGroupDiagram bigField.{u}).map f ≫ compHom T' = compHom T ≫ transSections f :=
  (genHom_comp (structSheaf baseRing.{u}) (Spec.map (𝟙 baseRing.{u})) (Spec.map_id _)
    (structSheafTrivialization baseRing.{u}) (stageHom T) (Spec.map (stageHom T)) (stage_w T)
    (transHom f) (stageHom T') (Spec.map (stageHom T')) (stage_w T') (trans_w f)).symm

/-- The quasi-coherence of the structure sheaf, at the spelling of the base stage that the
descent situation of Tag 01Z0 uses.  Instance synthesis does not see through
`collapse.system.obj (op collapse.base)` to `Spec baseRing`. -/
instance isQuasicoherent_structSheaf_collapse :
    SheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherent
      (R := ((collapse.{u}).system.obj (op (collapse.{u}).base)).ringCatSheaf)
      (structSheaf baseRing.{u}) :=
  inferInstanceAs ((structSheaf baseRing.{u}).IsQuasicoherent)

/-- The presheaf of Tag 03DS for the structure sheaf of the base stage. -/
abbrev cardPresheaf : PullbackSectionsPresheaf (Spec baseRing.{u}) (structSheaf baseRing.{u}) :=
  quasiCoherentPresheaf (Spec baseRing.{u}) (structSheaf baseRing.{u})

/-- The identification of the value of the presheaf at the stage `T` with the global sections there. -/
abbrev cardObjIso (T : Idx.{u}) :
    cardPresheaf.{u}.functor.obj (op (Over.mk (Spec.map (stageHom T)))) ≅
      Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (Spec.map (stageHom T))).obj (structSheaf baseRing.{u}), ⊤) :=
  cardPresheaf.{u}.objIso (op (Over.mk (Spec.map (stageHom T))))

/-- The diagram map of Tag 01Z0, read through `cardObjIso`.  This is `map_objIso`. -/
theorem cardMap_eq {T T' : Idx.{u}} (f : T ⟶ T') :
    (quasiCoherentPresheafFunctor (Spec baseRing.{u}) (structSheaf baseRing.{u})).map
        ((schemesOverBase collapse.{u}).map f)
      = (cardObjIso T).hom ≫ transSections f ≫ (cardObjIso T').inv := by
  rw [schemesOverBase_map f, transSections,
    pullbackSectionsMap_eq_functor (structSheaf baseRing.{u})
      (overHom (Spec.map (stageHom T)) (transHom f) (Spec.map (stageHom T')) (trans_w f))]
  simp
  rfl

/-- **The identification of the diagram of Tag 01Z0 with the diagram of stage rings**, before the
universe lift. -/
def groupDiagIso :
    stageGroupDiagram bigField.{u} ≅
      schemesOverBase collapse.{u} ⋙
        quasiCoherentPresheafFunctor (Spec baseRing.{u}) (structSheaf baseRing.{u}) :=
  NatIso.ofComponents (fun T => asIso (compHom T) ≪≫ (cardObjIso T).symm) (by
    intro T T' f
    refine Eq.trans ?_ (congrArg (fun m => (compHom T ≫ (cardObjIso T).inv) ≫ m)
      (cardMap_eq f)).symm
    change (stageGroupDiagram bigField.{u}).map f ≫ compHom T' ≫ (cardObjIso T').inv
      = (compHom T ≫ (cardObjIso T).inv) ≫
        (cardObjIso T).hom ≫ transSections f ≫ (cardObjIso T').inv
    simp only [Category.assoc, Iso.inv_hom_id_assoc]
    rw [← Category.assoc, compHom_naturality f, Category.assoc])

/-- **The identification**: the diagram of stagewise sections of Tag 01Z0 is the diagram of
stage rings. -/
def diagIso :
    pullbackSectionsDiagram collapse.{u} (structSheaf baseRing.{u}) ≅
      stageSectionsDiagram bigField.{u} :=
  Functor.isoWhiskerRight groupDiagIso.{u}.symm AddCommGrpCat.uliftFunctor.{u + 1, u}

/-- The cocone on the diagram of Tag 01Z0 whose apex is the field itself, obtained from
`Stacks.LimitSectionsCounterexample.fieldCocone` through the identification. -/
def cardCocone : Cocone (pullbackSectionsDiagram collapse.{u} (structSheaf baseRing.{u})) where
  pt := (fieldCocone bigField.{u}).pt
  ι := diagIso.{u}.hom ≫ (fieldCocone bigField.{u}).ι

/-- **The colimit of the diagram of Tag 01Z0 is not zero.**  Its leg at the base stage sends `1`
to `1`, through the identification. -/
theorem not_isZero_colimit_pullbackSectionsDiagram :
    ¬ IsZero (colimit (pullbackSectionsDiagram collapse.{u} (structSheaf baseRing.{u}))) := by
  intro hz
  have hι : colimit.ι (pullbackSectionsDiagram collapse.{u} (structSheaf baseRing.{u}))
      (⟨∅, le_refl _⟩ : Idx.{u}) = 0 := hz.eq_zero_of_tgt _
  have hleg : cardCocone.{u}.ι.app (⟨∅, le_refl _⟩ : Idx.{u}) = 0 := by
    rw [← colimit.ι_desc cardCocone.{u} (⟨∅, le_refl _⟩ : Idx.{u}), hι, zero_comp]
  have h0 : (fieldCocone bigField.{u}).ι.app (⟨∅, le_refl _⟩ : Idx.{u}) = 0 := by
    have : IsIso (diagIso.{u}.hom.app (⟨∅, le_refl _⟩ : Idx.{u})) :=
      inferInstanceAs (IsIso ((Functor.mapIso ((evaluation _ _).obj
        (⟨∅, le_refl _⟩ : Idx.{u})) diagIso.{u}).hom))
    rw [← cancel_epi (diagIso.{u}.hom.app (⟨∅, le_refl _⟩ : Idx.{u})), comp_zero]
    exact hleg
  have hone := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom h0 (ULift.up (1 : stage bigField.{u} ∅))
  rw [fieldCocone_ι_app_apply] at hone
  simp only [map_one, Subring.coe_one] at hone
  exact one_ne_zero (α := bigField.{u}) hone

/-- **The contradiction.**  For the descent situation `Stacks.LimitSectionsCounterexample.collapse`
  and the
structure sheaf of its base stage, the canonical map out of the filtered colimit of the stagewise
sections is *not* an isomorphism: the conclusion of Tag 01Z0 forces that colimit to be a zero object,
and the identification says it is the colimit of the stage rings, which is not. -/
theorem not_isIso_colimitDesc :
    ¬ IsIso (colimit.desc (pullbackSectionsDiagram collapse.{u} (structSheaf baseRing.{u}))
      (pullbackSectionsLimitCocone collapse.{u} (structSheaf baseRing.{u}))) :=
  fun h => not_isZero_colimit_pullbackSectionsDiagram.{u}
    (isZero_colimit_of_isIso_colimitDesc (structSheaf baseRing.{u}) h)

/-- **Tag 01Z0 is false.**  The conclusion of the tag, quantified over descent situations and
quasi-coherent modules as the tag states it — with the index a directed preorder in a universe
independent of the schemes', and no smallness assumption on the index — fails for
`Stacks.LimitSectionsCounterexample.collapse` and the structure sheaf of its base stage. -/
theorem not_card_01Z0 :
    ¬ ∀ {I : Type (u + 1)} [Preorder I] [IsDirected I (· ≤ ·)]
        (d : DescentSituation.{u + 1, u} I) (F : (d.system.obj (op d.base)).Modules)
        [F.IsQuasicoherent],
        IsIso (colimit.desc (pullbackSectionsDiagram d F) (pullbackSectionsLimitCocone d F)) :=
  fun h => not_isIso_colimitDesc.{u} (h collapse.{u} (structSheaf baseRing.{u}))

end Stacks.LimitSectionsIdentification

end
